  controlSentences:
  - Closes mountains spreadsheet at before weekdays.
  - Bridge maps sells attic platform flour appear bread.
  - Needs bakery green bread records nine attic.
  - Cedar for smells sells attic rooms mountains at.
  - Arrived river wood chess is.
  - Clocks recipe cedar rooms kitchen river was.
  - Dries budget sells rooms sound early meeting bridge records.
  - Bakery roads attic small faster paper sunrise quietly nine.
  - Opens sells on maps jazz her.
  - Tea umbrella her blue rooms.
  - Purple paper library thursday old inward.
  - Before cedar postcards needs copper trains library closes.
  - Needs arrived steep before turntable river rooms.
  - Library sunset like show paper sells.
  - Bakery window bread ink out tea steep.
  - Attic thursday tea kitchen.
  - Rooms sunrise weekdays old inward the monthly steep like.
  - Opens long copper slowly.
  - Paper attic flour two.
  - Chair to her mountains yesterday paper.
  - The museum opens at nine on weekdays.
  - Blue paint dries faster in summer.
  - Trains leave from the north platform.
  - The recipe needs two cups of flour.
  - Chess clocks were invented long ago.
  - Her umbrella is on the kitchen chair.
  - The meeting moved to Thursday afternoon.
  - Violins sound warmer in small rooms.
  - Postcards arrived from the coast yesterday.
  - The printer is out of ink again.
  - Mountains appear purple at sunset.
  - The library closes early on holidays.
  - Copper wires carry the signal inward.
  - Old maps show roads that vanished.
  - The bakery sells bread before sunrise.
  - A spreadsheet tracks the monthly budget.
  - Jazz records spin on the turntable.
  - The bridge was painted last spring.
  - Tea leaves steep for three minutes.
  - The attic smells like cedar wood.
